Let \[f(x) =
\begin{cases}
x^2+2 &\text{if } x<n, \\
2x+5 &\text{if }x\ge{n}.
\end{cases}
\]If the graph $y=f(x)$ is continuous, find the sum of all possible values of $n$.

Let
\[f(a,b) = \left\{
\renewcommand{\arraystretch}{3}
\begin{array}{cl}
\dfrac{ab - a + 2}{2a} & \text{if $a + b \le 3$}, \\
\dfrac{ab - b - 2}{-2b} & \text{if $a + b > 3$}.
\end{array}
\renewcommand{\arraystretch}{1}
\right.\]Find $f(2,1) + f(2,4).$
